# mcp-ready-under-load - the MCP test client's readiness deadline is WIDENED by
# the contention factor the harness publishes, instead of racing a fixed 10s.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-plugin-concurrency-is-pinned-to-a-ci-constant AC-1, at
# the process boundary. cmdMcp (internal/test/cli/cmd_mcp.go) multiplies its
# --timeout by runner.ChildParallelFactor (internal/test/runner/parallel.go),
# which reads ze.test.parallel-factor out of the environment the runner handed
# this child. The failure message names the deadline the client actually waited,
# so the assertion is on the value under test and not on an elapsed time a busy
# box can perturb.
#
# The factor is set HERE rather than inherited from the suite's own -p, because
# the inherited value is 3 under `make ze-functional-plugin-test` and 1 under
# `ze-test bgp plugin mcp-ready-under-load`, and a test whose expected value
# changes with the way it is run cannot assert one. 5 is neither of those, so a
# pass cannot come from the runner's own value leaking through.
#
# This half proves the CONSUMER across a real exec. The producer half -- that
# the runner publishes its own parallelFactor and not a constant -- is pinned by
# TestParallelFactorEnvPublishesTheRunnerFactor
# (internal/test/runner/runner_exec_util_test.go), which cannot cross a process
# boundary, exactly as this file cannot see the runner's internals.
#
# PREVENTS: the 10s readiness deadline returning as a fixed constant. Six of the
# 665 plugin tests failed in one 32-way run on nothing but
# `MCP server not ready: no listener on 127.0.0.1:<port> after 10s`.
#
# Port 1 is privileged and unbound, so the readiness probe can only run its
# deadline out. No daemon is started: what is under test is how long the client
# waits for one, not what it does when one answers.

option=env:var=ze.test.parallel-factor:value=5
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test mcp --port 1 --timeout 200ms:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=MCP server not ready
expect=stderr:contains=no listener on 127.0.0.1:1 after 1s
